 "adjudications": {
  "Scale": "RECLASSIFIED from failing: the round-40 record (Android Modifier.scale clips to parent at >=1.5, 0.69) is STALE — the mechanism does not exist in current code (Modifier.scale = graphicsLayer clip=false; no clipToBounds on the fixture path) and the clip hypothesis was quantitatively refuted (synthetic clip models score 0.69-0.81 vs the measured 0.996+). This run: V_half 0.9963 / V_one_half 0.9944 / V_two 1.0 — passing.",
  "BackgroundImage": "BI_none wave-4 0.9281 was the pre-block-font label artifact; solo wave-5 run = 1.0. Remaining sub-0.995 signal is BI_radial/BI_rep_linear gradient color drift (deltaE p95 ~6-9), separate small divergence.",
  "TextDecorationSkipInk": "Chromium skip-ink gaps measured at exactly 17px per decorated variant (2.0% of Android-web divergent pixels, deltaSSIM 0.0019) — WALL; per-character advance-subtraction emulation simulated SSIM-NEGATIVE (0.881->0.8774), do not implement.",
  "TextTransform": "FullWidth/FullSizeKana variants are VACUOUS on the Latin corpus — Chromium (the reference) renders them as no-ops; natives deliberately mirror. Exhausted-variant, do not implement toFullWidth.",
  "MarginTrim": "The 0.832 is 100% missing native BLOCK MARGIN-COLLAPSE (CSS2 8.3.1 sibling max + collapse-through), NOT trim: margin-trim itself is unimplemented in Chromium (CSS.supports false) so all three platforms correctly no-op it; the trim mechanism is blocked-platform (reference engine lacks support). Wave-6 implements the collapse emulation.",
  "BorderImageSlice": "Apparent -0.046 regression is band-shuffling: the real slice variants improved (Fill 0.853->0.986 after the web fill fix); the min moved to the intentionally-named V_svg_source_blocked_native_no_svg_decode blocked-platform variant (0.807).",
  "AndroidFirstLine": "NEW SEAM: iOS-Android-worst typography cluster (InitialLetter 0.911, LineHeight_Rem_2 0.876, LineSnap 0.890, TextAlign_Center 0.893, FontLanguageOverride 0.875) diverges ONLY on Android and only on the FIRST text line (InitialLetter: iOS-web 0.9907, divergence rows 24-42, line 2 pixel-identical) — shared Android first-baseline/half-leading mechanism, wave-6 lane investigating."
